      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Settlers first arrived in 1855, and by 1856 a town was founded just south and west of a ham‑shaped lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ham_Lake%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Swedish Evangelical Lutheran Church, founded in 1872, is still standing in the city and is on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.hamlakemn.gov/about/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlers found the soil well‑suited to farming as it wasn’t as rocky as they had been accustomed to in Norway and Sweden.",
